# Checkpoint2: selective magnitude, unresolved mechanism
New retrospective result: at exact2h PMP22delta1.962log2 exceeds99.84% of1276 baseline-matched references; median-reference residual1.740. Alternative reference sets retain >99.6th percentile. Mere sign reversal is common (31.8% matched genes MEFup/NIHdown), so claim must be unusual MAGNITUDE, not unique sign. This is new within-dataset inference, not an independent result or new causal mechanism.

Anomaly-directed follow-up chosen before next computation: (1) avoid response eligibility bias by using baseline-only>=10 and explicitly clipping treatment/control TPM to4 as authors' stated analysis does; deposited matrix contains0 and values below4, so >4 is our analytical eligibility threshold, not proof of source quantification failure. Original script's positive-value arm is NOT a clipping sensitivity; label precisely. Compare full baseline-only cohort, outcome>4 restriction, actual clip4, median-centering. Because uniform sample scaling only adds constants to log-fold change, target-versus-reference median delta and percentile are invariant for fixed eligible set; demonstrate without claiming absolute synthesis.
(2) same1uM MEF WT/KO timecourse using own genotype controls at1,2,5,8h: deltaWT-minusKO. Freeze descriptive analysis over all eligible genes plus two-dimensional WT/KO baseline matching to Pmp22, +/-1log2 and nearest250. One library/condition; no clone/rescue or population p-value. Primary mechanistic question: does relative Pmp22 increase require WT context or persist inKO? All raw MEF values inherited/exposed; fully retrospective. This cannot isolate translation from RNA changes.
(3) audit gene-class alternative using source TableS5 MEF late-induction set, since Pmp22 belongs to that published set. This is outcome-selected within the same data; it is a conditional descriptive check against the published program, not independent validation. Test NIH response distribution and shared2h contextdelta within all eligible late-cluster genes and baseline-matched late-cluster subset. Do not claim class independence or use cluster choice to manufacture significance.

Compare with external acquisition: replicated dose-by-cell footprint plus RNA is decisive but not located. Current same-study KO/program tests are feasible and distinguish dependence on WT/program membership at low cost. After them, inspect closest primary prior work and independent public design for a valid next validation; no retrospective resealing.
